From the look of the code, it appears that the bone files will be different
not only for different machines, but also for different sets compilation
parameters.  Trying to make bone-file exchange possible is going to require
a lot of work.  However, it is conceivable that a whole bunch of people
who are using the same type of machine, say SparcStations, get together
and agree to rebuild their nethack using one set of parameters, under the
same version of OS and C compiler + libraries.  They can then exchange
bone files freely among themselves.  The question now is how to organize.
